  // Log the key that was pressed
  console.log(event.key);
});
```

3. This code will log every key that is pressed by the user to the browser's console. The attacker can then access this console to collect the user's keystrokes.

4. To make the keylogger more difficult to detect, the attacker might obfuscate the code or hide it in an image or other non-obvious location. They might also use techniques like cross-site scripting (XSS) to inject the code into the site without the user's knowledge.

